  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/528863">Definition <span data-tag="528863">5.2.1.1</span>.</a>functor!associated to a correspondencecorrespondence!associated functor Let $p: \calM \rightarrow \Delta ^1$ be a Cartesian fibration, and suppose given equivalences of $\infty $-categories $h_0: \calC \rightarrow p^{-1} \{ 0\} $ and $h_1: \calD \rightarrow p^{-1} \{ 1\} $. We will say that a functor $g: \calD \rightarrow \calC $ is <em>associated to $\calM $</em> if there is a commutative diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { \calD \times \Delta ^1 \ar [dr] \ar [rr]^{s} &amp;  &amp;  \calM \ar [dl] \\ &amp;  \Delta ^1 &amp;  } \]
</div>
  <p> such that $s| \calD \times \{ 1\}  = h_1$, $s| \calD \times \{ 0\}  = h_0 \circ g$, and $s| \{ x\}  \times \Delta ^1$ is a $p$-Cartesian edge of $\calM $ for every object $x$ of $\calD $. </p>
